  (text "POWER OR-ing into the shared +5V node - two reverse-blocking paths:\n  USB path : VBUS (+5V_USB) -> U802 LM66100 ideal diode (CE tied to VOUT).\n             95 mOhm, ~48 mV @ 0.5 A.  USB is capped at 500 mA so 1.5 A is ample.\n  Buck path: MP2307 out (+5V_BUCK) -> U803 LM74700 ideal-diode controller +\n             Q803 AO3400A N-FET (on the power sheet).  FET-limited (~5 A),\n             ~53 mV @ 1.9 A.  Sized above the ~1.9 A worst-case +5V budget\n             (LED strip at the 1 A JST-SH cap + ESP32 WiFi + RX + GPS + sensors).\n  Each path blocks reverse current into its own source; highest input wins +5V.\n  +5V rail ~= 4.95 V from either source.  FB divider stays on +5V_BUCK so the\n  buck regulates its own 5.0 V and does not cross-couple to VBUS.\n  ERC: +5V now has one power-output pin (U802.VOUT); pin_map[8][8] is back to Error.\n\nRUNS on USB power alone (~500 mA, USB2.0):\n  STM32 + gyro + baro + blackbox flash, RC receiver, GPS, buzzer (brief),\n  ESP32 for firmware flash / config (WiFi TX bursts may brown out on 500 mA).\nDOES NOT run on USB alone:\n  4-in-1 ESC / motors (VBAT only - no props spin on USB, by design),\n  long WS2812 LED strip (amps), anything on the raw VBAT rail.\nVBAT_SENSE reads ~0 V with no LiPo connected - expected."
    (at 30 150 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "fc38104a-38eb-4e20-ac6d-b4ab8c9d72c4")
  )
